@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] inference-exact-execution-authority
Admission and renewal MUST authenticate a dedicated Ziggy credential, serialize
against current host and VM state, and bind the exact placement and execution
epoch. Customer and unknown profiles MUST deny admission, identity authorization
and renewal, including previously admitted requests. Neither user headers, provider keys nor cached VM ownership confer authority.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:accounting] inference-metadata-only-idempotence
Request IDs MUST be unique durable admissions before provider effects. Completion
MUST be immutable and idempotent, attributed to the admitted VM owner; a replay
matches only an exactly equal stored completion, and PostgreSQL MUST refuse a
stored completion outside the closed wire key set. Missing usage MUST remain unknown. Prompts, responses, tools and upstream error bodies
MUST never enter persisted records or diagnostics.
